Description: NimbusOS look: the Nimbus Dark theme everywhere
 The visual identity of NimbusOS, from boot to desktop:
  - GRUB theme, used through /etc/default/grub.d/10-nimbusos.cfg, which also
    names the boot entries "NimbusOS" and adds the boot splash;
  - Plymouth boot splash with a passphrase prompt for encrypted disks;
  - SDDM login theme "nimbus" (Qt 6 greeter);
  - Calamares installer branding;
  - Plasma global theme "Nimbus Dark" (org.nimbusos.desktop) with a floating
    bottom panel, the NimbusDark colour scheme and the Nimbus Sky wallpaper;
  - system-wide defaults in /etc/xdg: colours and accent, Papirus-Dark icons,
    Inter and JetBrains Mono, KWin blur and translucency.
 .
 The defaults in /etc/xdg apply to every user who hasn't changed the setting
 themselves, so theme updates reach existing users too.
